{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":68865,"duration_api_ms":81266,"num_turns":8,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c86959da-586e-42fb-8f4f-252924e81c25","total_cost_usd":0.37742620000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25853,"cache_read_input_tokens":184554,"output_tokens":2287,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25853,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":31,"outputTokens":2415,"cacheReadInputTokens":86832,"cacheCreationInputTokens":36455,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.06635795,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":2287,"cacheReadInputTokens":184554,"cacheCreationInputTokens":25853,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.31106825,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept the vacuous debug_assert fix. Reject all others: the test tolerance is justified by observed ratios (~0.858), the test file is already tracked, the tracing metrics have already been split into tan_oxidized_mg vs nitrate_produced_mg_n, and alkalinity_produced_meq already exists in the output struct and engine tracing.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-f86e4833","decision":"accept","rationale":"The analysis is correct. alk_budget is initialized to state.water.alkalinity_meq_total (line 218), then decremented with .max(0.0) clamping (lines 296, 351). By the time the debug_assert fires at line 352, alk_budget is guaranteed to be in [0, initial_value], so the check alk_budget <= initial_value + EPSILON is trivially true regardless of costs. This is a real defect — the assert provides no protection against over-deduction. Replacing it with a pre-clamp check (e.g., aob_alk_cost + comammox_alk_cost <= state.water.alkalinity_meq_total + EPSILON) or removing it entirely would be correct."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-1cbd2690","decision":"reject","rationale":"The planner reports the actual observed ratio is ~0.858 of the stoichiometric constant, which means tightening the lower bound to 0.90 would cause a false test failure. The 0.80 bound accommodates the real model behavior where biomass growth diverts more TAN than the simple ~5% comment suggests. Additionally, the test already has a separate, tighter check comparing alk_consumed directly to no2_no3_gain * constant. The current tolerance is appropriate for the model's actual dynamics."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-0f6e9beb","decision":"reject","rationale":"Factually incorrect. git ls-files confirms crates/tank_core/tests/nitrification_alkalinity.rs is already tracked in version control. The amendment's premise — that the file is untracked and missing from diffs — does not hold in the current tree."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7ee0abfa","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment describes a stale state. The code now exposes two separate metrics: tan_oxidized_mg (AOB + comammox TAN oxidation, the alkalinity basis) and nitrate_produced_mg_n (NOB + comammox nitrate production). Engine tracing at lines 247-251 records both distinctly alongside alkalinity_consumed_meq. There is no 'total_mg_n_nitrified' conflation — the diagnostics are already internally consistent when nitrite accumulates."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-aff4afaf","decision":"reject","rationale":"The reusable surface already exists. NitrogenCycleOutput has an alkalinity_produced_meq field (line 34) with a net_alkalinity_delta_meq() method (line 46). Engine tracing exports both alkalinity_consumed_meq and alkalinity_produced_meq (lines 252-258) plus the net delta (line 278-280). The denitrification constant is defined and the output schema is ready — future E4b work only needs to set alkalinity_produced_meq to a non-zero value. No API/schema change is required."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"94695d7c-bbc6-499a-bbfe-289484647017"}
